1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:10,460
With the trend of urbanization, it is vitally important for city residents to develop a stronger love for nature.
随着城市化的推进，城市居民培养对自然更深厚的热爱至关重要。

2
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:20,980
Surrounded by concrete buildings, many people now spend most of their time indoors and seldom notice the changing seasons, let alone the birds and trees around them.
被混凝土建筑包围，如今许多人大部分时间都待在室内，很少留意季节的变换，更不用说身边的鸟儿和树木了。

3
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:26,380
A deeper love for nature benefits both individuals and the city as a whole.
对自然更深的热爱既有益于个人，也有益于整个城市。

4
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:32,470
For one thing, time spent in green spaces relieves stress and refreshes the mind.
一方面，在绿地中度过的时光能缓解压力、让头脑焕然一新。

5
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:40,420
After a busy week, a walk in a park or along a river can do more for our mood than hours of scrolling through our phones.
忙碌了一周之后，去公园或沿着河边散散步，对我们心情的改善可能比花几个小时刷手机还要大。

6
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:46,600
For another, people who cherish nature are more willing to protect it in their daily lives.
另一方面，珍爱自然的人在日常生活中更愿意保护它。

7
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:53,920
They tend to sort their waste, save water and use public transportation, making the city cleaner and more livable.
他们往往会进行垃圾分类、节约用水、乘坐公共交通，让城市变得更加干净、更加宜居。

8
00:00:54,720 --> 00:01:06,850
To nurture this love, city governments should build more parks and green spaces in every neighborhood, and schools can organize outdoor activities so that children learn to observe plants and animals.
为了培养这份热爱，城市政府应在每个社区修建更多公园和绿地，学校则可以组织户外活动，让孩子们学会观察动植物。

9
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:13,280
Residents, too, can start simply by stepping outside and appreciating the natural world.
居民们也可以简单地从走出家门、欣赏大自然做起。

10
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:18,690
After all, a city that respects nature is a better home for everyone.
毕竟，一座尊重自然的城市对每个人来说都是更好的家园。
